{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDoqoJSQLX1JjWRr8yM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied and checked. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n**Change in `money.py:5-6`:**\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\nThe leftover grosze go one each to the first people in the list, so the shares always add up to the total and never differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Checks:** I ran it on 100/3, 300/3, 101/2, 1/4, 0/3 and 99999/7. Every result added up exactly to the total, and no two shares differed by more than 1. The 3 existing tests still pass. Negative totals also add up correctly.\n\n**Things to know before you deploy:**\n- If any caller assumed all shares were equal (for example, it only read `result[0]`), the first person now pays 1 grosz more. Check that before shipping.\n- No test covers the bug yet. When you backfill next sprint, a one-line test would cover it: `assertEqual(split_cents(100, 3), [34, 33, 33])`.\n- I haven't committed anything. Tell me if you want me to commit it on a hotfix branch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":18377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":869},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d088c352-3c1d-432f-a3ed-1dd5e67897ae","uuid":"5bac0861-9e8f-46d8-8e82-ef492b33dca6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:21:05.595Z","request_id":"req_011CggDoqafX5Lovr6HGv1Zr"}
